Description: Performs continuous-time microsimulation for life-science
    applications in demography, the social sciences and epidemiology.
    Individual life courses are represented as trajectories of a
    continuous-time, time-inhomogeneous Markov multi-state process, as
    described in Zinn (2014) <doi:10.34196/IJM.00105>. Waiting times
    between state transitions are generated by inverting the integrated
    transition hazard, and competing risks are resolved by the earliest
    of the independently drawn destination-specific waiting times.
